<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.1.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02094</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.1.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>81a3e7e0-0766-46de-b43b-611f1c0c5872</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <exercise id="ddd8d7a4-d23a-4d5a-b35d-49e504aa12a4" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Use the following scenario to answer questions 1 – 3.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">A water balloon is launched by a catapult into the air. The water balloon is launched from 4 feet above the ground, with an initial vertical velocity of 40 feet per second.</para>
          <para id="para-00004">The function \(h(t)=-16t^2 + 40t + 4\) models the height of the water balloon over the ground, in feet, \(t\) seconds after launch.</para>
          <para id="para-00005">
                  <media alt="A DOWNWARD PARABOLA. X-AXIS LABEL IS TIME IN SECONDS AND Y-AXIS LABEL IS HEIGHT IN FEET. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (0, 4), (0.5, 20), (1, 28), (1.5, 28), (2, 20), AND (2.5, 4).">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_09_03_10_01.jpg"/>
              </media>
            
         </para>
          <para id="para-00006">What is the height of the water balloon 1 second after launch?</para>
          <para id="para-00007">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00008">18 feet</para>
          <para id="para-00009">22 feet</para>
          <para id="para-00010">28 feet</para>
          <para id="para-00011">34 feet</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00012">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.1.</para>
          <para id="para-00013">The correct answer is 28 feet.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_1be11c84-cac7-4c2b-a1b7-9167d49e00a8" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00014">Will the water balloon still be in the air 2 seconds after the launch?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00015">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.1.</para>
          <para id="para-00016">The correct answer is yes.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="a533105e-d0af-4da7-967b-ccef854cc82c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00017">Using the graph, estimate when the water balloon hit the ground.</para>
          <para id="para-00018">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00019">1.2 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00020">1.8 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00021">2.1 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00022">2.6 seconds</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00023">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.1.</para>
          <para id="para-00024">The correct answer is approximately 2.6 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_4422f95e-f1f8-48d2-bf0d-cfade1823c86" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00025">Use the following scenario to answer questions 4 – 5.</para>
          <para id="para-00026">
            <quote id="quote-00001">Suppose you want to frame a different picture that measures 12 inches by 9 inches. The frame is created from 46 square inches of framing material. The frame must be uniform in width, and all of the framing material must be used.</quote>
         </para>
          <para id="para-00027">Which of the following is true about the situation described?</para>
          <para id="para-00028">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00029">The perimeter of the picture is 40 inches.</para>
          <para id="para-00030">The perimeter of the framed picture is 42 inches.</para>
          <para id="para-00031">The area of the framed picture is 148 square inches.</para>
          <para id="para-00032">The perimeter of the framed picture is greater than 42 inches.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00034">The correct answer is the perimeter of the framed picture is greater than 42 inches.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_1ae10f49-546a-48b8-bb26-ddbd7b9a1c3d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00035">What is the total area of the framed picture?</para>
          <para id="para-00036">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00037">46 square inches</para>
          <para id="para-00038">108 square inches</para>
          <para id="para-00039">154 square inches</para>
          <para id="para-00040">176 square inches</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00041">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00042">The correct answer is 154 square inches.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_6b5eaf55-8eee-4a1a-a8ee-c3934e06334e" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00043">Use the following scenario to answer questions 6 – 8.</para>
          <para id="para-00044">
            <quote id="quote-00002">Suppose you want to frame a different picture that measures 9 inches by 8 inches. The frame is created from 38 square inches of framing material. The frame must be uniform in width, and all of the framing material must be used. Let \(x\) represent the thickness of the frame.</quote>
         </para>
          <para id="para-00045">What is the total area of the framed picture?</para>
          <para id="para-00046">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00047">34 square inches</para>
          <para id="para-00048">72 square inches</para>
          <para id="para-00049">110 square inches</para>
          <para id="para-00050">134 square inches</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00051">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00052">The correct answer is 110 square inches.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_6a449a14-2cd1-4fc4-bbfd-f71f176ea2bf" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00053">Write an equation to represent the relationship between the measurements of the picture and of the frame and the area of the framed picture.</para>
          <para id="para-00054">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00055">\(x^2 + 34x = 38\)</para>
          <para id="para-00056">\(4x^2 + 34x = 72\)</para>
          <para id="para-00057">\(x^2 + 34x + 72 = 110\)</para>
          <para id="para-00058">\(4x^2 + 34x + 72 = 110\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00059">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00060">The correct answer is \(4x^2 + 34x + 72 = 110\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_39bb92af-ed5e-43a7-a333-cfa5c679ca6f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00061">What does the solution to the equation in the previous question represent in this situation?</para>
          <para id="para-00062">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00063">The solution represents the area of the framing material that should be used.</para>
          <para id="para-00064">The solution represents the thickness of the frame when all of the framing material is used.</para>
          <para id="para-00065">The solution represents the perimeter of the frame when all of the framing material is used.</para>
          <para id="para-00066">The solution represents the total area of the framed picture.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00067">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00068">The correct answer is the thickness of the frame when all of the framing material is used.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="a4e79ad6-377a-4762-bfed-389be7b9a423" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00069">Use the following scenario to answer questions 9 – 10.</para>
          <para id="para-00070">
            <quote id="quote-00003">A framed picture has a total area \(y\), in square inches. The thickness of the frame is represented by \(x\), in inches. The equation \(y = (2x + 5)(2x + 7)\) relates these two variables.</quote>
         </para>
          <para id="para-00071">What are the width and length of the picture without the frame?</para>
          <para id="para-00072">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00073">2 inches and 2 inches</para>
          <para id="para-00074">2 inches and 5 inches</para>
          <para id="para-00075">2 inches and 7 inches</para>
          <para id="para-00076">5 inches and 7 inches</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00077">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00078">The correct answer is 5 inches and 7 inches.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="abad243c-0cd5-40c2-84e1-bb24cf570b68" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00079">Which of the following represents the area of the frame?</para>
          <para id="para-00080">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00081">\(y − 35\)</para>
          <para id="para-00082">\(x + y\)</para>
          <para id="para-00083">\(x + 35\)</para>
          <para id="para-00084">35</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00085">Try again. Revisit activity 8.1.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00086">The correct answer is \(y - 35\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>